{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791198768,"nonce":"ZCGpHZPL1cPSNQtGNPXT12GaUQQ=","title":"Deploy Website cannot be re-run: pages artifact name collides across attempts","message":"Run 37298852052 (e6838017) failed at actions/deploy-pages@v5 with \"No artifacts named github-pages were found\" right after upload-pages-artifact succeeded in the same job — a GitHub-side lookup failure (1 failure in the last 60 runs; the next workflow_run deploy on the same commit succeeded).\n\nRe-running it then failed deterministically: \"Multiple artifacts named github-pages were unexpectedly found for this workflow run. Artifact count is 2.\" A re-run keeps attempt 1's artifact, so the action's own advice (\"re-run the deployment\") can never work.\n\nFix: name the artifact github-pages-${{ github.run_attempt }} in both upload-pages-artifact (`name`) and deploy-pages (`artifact_name`).","files":null}]}